# Reference oracle (reference/python). Runtime outputs are cwd-relative: run from this
# directory and they land under data/ here (data/cache/*.parquet|*.npz|*.joblib,
# data/db/*.sqlite, data/logs/, data/health.json, data/snapshots/, data/reports/), and
# tools/investigations/fetch_realdata.py downloads nflverse inputs to data/realdata/.
# Nothing under data/ is source, and real third-party data is never committed.
/data/
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
*.parquet
*.joblib
# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
.env
# run_demo.py output when GRID_DEMO_OUT points here
grid_recovery.png
grid_focus_qb.png
# The committed golden master must stay tracked even if a broader rule is ever added.
!tests/grid/golden/snapshot.npz
